{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1459486-the-fae-s-lack-of-empathy","id":1459486,"title":"The Fae's Lack of Empathy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-09T19:13:42-07:00","id":1459486,"title":"The Fae's Lack of Empathy","content":"I'm getting the impression from reading the very first description of the true Fae in 2e that their disregard for others,their habit of seeing everyone from our world as playthings is a learned behavior.<br /> Not a inherent part of them<br /> Do you think I may be right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T20:02:08-07:00","id":1459491,"title":"","content":"Elaborate, possibly with the specific description in question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T21:54:59-07:00","id":1459496,"title":"","content":"They are the literal embodiment of the end conclusion of solipsism, unable to distinguish between Self and Other.<br /> <br /> Have you ever fought an imaginary enemy in your head? Made them bleed, made them suffer, because that helped you not be mean and horrible in action at best, because you were bored at worst?<br /> <br /> The True Fae find changelings holding them accountable for their actions similar to the Jason Hookhands in your head turning around and accusing you of making them like this-of course they did, but it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;All the world's a !stage!, and all the men and women merely players&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;They say idle hands are the devil's playthings, but there is something far, far, worse. An idle mind is the devil's playhouse. A !stage! for the most vapid, horrible, and destructive stories to be made real...&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-10-2021, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T06:19:01-07:00","id":1459548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1459486-the-fae-s-lack-of-empathy?p=1459491#post1459491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elaborate, possibly with the specific description in question?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think on page 63 of the codebook pdf,the 2e one. It says they Dont care about others because they are &quot; the only subject on a world of objects&quot; and it made me wonder if they can unlearn that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T06:20:31-07:00","id":1459549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1459486-the-fae-s-lack-of-empathy?p=1459496#post1459496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are the literal embodiment of the end conclusion of solipsism, unable to distinguish between Self and Other.<br /> <br /> Have you ever fought an imaginary enemy in your head? Made them bleed, made them suffer, because that helped you not be mean and horrible in action at best, because you were bored at worst?<br /> <br /> The True Fae find changelings holding them accountable for their actions similar to the Jason Hookhands in your head turning around and accusing you of making them like this-of course they did, but it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;All the world's a !stage!, and all the men and women merely players&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;They say idle hands are the devil's playthings, but there is something far, far, worse. An idle mind is the devil's playhouse. A !stage! for the most vapid, horrible, and destructive stories to be made real...&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure I get it,are you saying they see the people they turn into changelings as extensions of their imagination?<br /> Edit: just looked up what solipsism is. I get it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 09-10-2021, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T14:30:30-07:00","id":1465180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally hold the headcanon that True Fae become as Solipstic as they do because of the fact that any possible 'beings' they might come across generally tend to be little more than animated parts of themselves, be they Actors, parts of a group of Wisps, or the denizens of a Realm. That, and they generally aren't given much chance to learn how to rise above their instincts.<br /> <br /> Thus, let me try to spin something here, using the Game of Immortals from <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/57384/Equinox-Road?term=equinox+road\" target=\"_blank\">Equinox Road</a>, and the above headcanon, as a base foundation/set of assumptions for the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Say that a Motley of Changelings makes their way into Faerie and somehow stumbles upon a freshly 'spawned' 'clutch' of Gentry. Thanks to a combination of shenanigans, misunderstandings, noodle incidents, and poorly worded turns of phrase, the changelings somehow end up adopting the Others as their collective children, taking them back to earth.<br /> <br /> Over the following years, the group of Gentry learn how to rise above their instincts and recognise other people as <i>people</i>, rather than as Objects to be acted upon by the lone Subject (aka themselves). When they eventually end up moving the majority of themselves back into Arcadia, this capability eventually leads them to becoming the longest-lived group in the entirety of their realm.<br /> <br /> \u2026I think that I <i>might</i> have somehow created the basis for a near-unique C:tL story.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is missing the fact that too much time in Ironside will <i>kill</i> a True Fae.<br /> <br /> Also, don't post links to the whole PDFs of books-pay your authors, folks.<br /> <br /> EDIT: realized my post still had the link to the pirated material, so we changed it to the DTRPG page for the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-24-2021, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:01:31-07:00","id":1465185,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please do not share pirated material.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T16:09:56-07:00","id":1465202,"title":"","content":"Did something in 2nd Ed superceded Equinox Road on True Fae? Because it does answer the thread's main question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T16:29:43-07:00","id":1465205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1459486-the-fae-s-lack-of-empathy?p=1465202#post1465202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did something in 2nd Ed superceded Equinox Road on True Fae? Because it does answer the thread's main question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the &quot;it&quot; is Equinox Road, um, no. It was Equinox Road I cited for the solipsism-driven answer.<br /> <br /> The response in question, not related to the facilitation of piracy, is that the True Fae aren't, strictly speaking, rehabilitable creatures-the response for trying to do so neglecting the fact that the True Fae can only abide so much time in Ironside/the normal world before they die. Charlatans might be able to claw up a form of humanity to keep as theirs, but putting asides the &quot;can't spend meaningful neccessary time in a place that is not the part of the self&quot; problem, the Bargains that allow the True Fae to Be also don't really ultimately allow for a nuanced capacity for distinction between Self and Other beyond what is reached anyways.<br /> <br /> The facilitation of piracy angle is that Cooper shared the whole Equinox Road PDF in a link, which, asides from being a dick move, is also very against the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T17:31:11-07:00","id":1465217,"title":"","content":"I'm not really talking about the post, although I did read it before deletion, I'm talking about Equinox Road itself. I know the solipsism part is from there, but I was initially shy from talking more here because I didn't read 2nd Ed yet, but I did read ER.<br /> <br /> To be honest I saw the link and assumed it was to some other post or to DTRPG or whatever so I didn't noticed it was to a pirate PDF. I won't discuss piracy here because it is more complex than that, but it is a crime and against the rules of any forum anyway, there is no point, here's not the place, period.<br /> <br /> Much less putting a pirate copy in a forum kept by the very publisher. Wtf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T17:35:08-07:00","id":1465220,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ER answers the Why behind Why The True Fae Don't Have Empathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T00:08:46-07:00","id":1465247,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t realise it was pirated material, so apologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T01:00:49-07:00","id":1465254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1459486-the-fae-s-lack-of-empathy?p=1465247#post1465247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn\u2019t realise it was pirated material, so apologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>What defines piracy is the right of distribution. Even if you have a legit PDF, you can't let others copy it or it is piracy. If the site where the PDF is hosted isn't the official publisher or a retailer, then offering the link <i><u>is piracy on itself</u></i>.<br /> <br /> The fine details of the law are complicated, so the host sites are usually legit enough <i>for personal backups</i>. Don't sweat it. You can discuss your opinion on the matter in general if you want.<br /> <br /> But to be direct to the point, if you link or direct people in any way to free downloads here you legally compromise the forum itself. So just don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T06:19:51-07:00","id":1465387,"title":"","content":"The thing is, if a True Fae even begins to adopt human qualities like empathy, chances he gets exiled by his peers or even rejected by Faerie itself.<br /> Like with the Grey Gentlemen from Momo or the Auditors from Discworld, to become &quot;human&quot; is to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 10-26-2021, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T09:27:24-07:00","id":1465414,"title":"","content":"I think that a good example is the IT of the book Flatland.<br /> In short, the main character, a square in a bidimensional world, tries to adress a point creature.<br /> But the zero dimensional point is so self absorbed in his self contained world that it simply CANNOT contemplate the existence of other things.<br /> It is perfect and whole, everything is part of it, so it can do everything it wants with its whole universe.<br /> Even if something tries to enter in its world it simply doesn t notice any difference or change","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 10-26-2021, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T09:39:44-07:00","id":1465415,"title":"","content":"Yes, I wouldn't say it is completely impossible as ER does hint to a very faint possibility and have a sample Exile, although I don't remember the details very well and my copy isn't at hand right now.<br /> <br /> But it is a BIG thing for any True Fae to even begin the <i><u>possibility</u></i> of learning empathy and normal feelings (I won't say humans because they're far even from many animals), and extremely dangerous. Our world is even more dangerous to them than Faerie is for humans at a long stay, and the Hedge is just better enough to stave off death IIRC.<br /> <br /> With all the probability it would require the Fae to already be an exile and completely cut off from its world, and even then the result is kind of messy as this isn't an actual Changeling, rules aside, not even a Goblin but a completely different being never meant to be human in the first place.<br /> <br /> And another problem with the idea of &quot;adopting a fresh clutch of Gentry&quot; is what &quot;young&quot; means here. Fresh or not, they're not children in an animal sense, they never were. They're already full-fledged &quot;living stories&quot;, their Titles already manifest as adults unless the Title itself is child-like or something. It is important to grasp just how much <b><u><i>Other</i></u></b> they are.<br /> <br /> Even bringing them to Earth means exiling them and exposing them to harm, so expecting anything is expecting too much. May it come to work? Maybe, but it would be far weirder a tale than it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}